 "vision": {
  "doc": "The image tower (HF model.visual.*, bf16, excluded from the Quark quantization) -> the internal names the GGUF mmproj uses (llama.cpp's clip converter, qwen3vl_merger), so the encoder plan (vision/encoder.py) is shared. Matrices are read natively as bf16 (llama.cpp rounds them to f16; the native read is closer to the checkpoint); biases, norms and the position table are f32 in the mmproj, so they are prepared copies (bf16 -> f32 at load, op copy); the conv3d patch embedding is read natively from its HF layout [E, 3, T=2, P, P] (kernel layout hf3d: the converter's patch_embd.weight / .1 are the two temporal taps).",
  "family": "qwen3vl_merger", "config": "vision_config", "prefix": "model.visual.",
  "img_begin": "<|vision_start|>", "img_end": "<|vision_end|>",
  "eps": 1e-06,
  "preprocess_defaults": {"image_mean": [0.5, 0.5, 0.5], "image_std": [0.5, 0.5, 0.5]},
  "config_keys": {"patch": "patch_size", "E": "hidden_size", "NH": "num_heads", "ffn": "intermediate_size", "layers": "depth",
                  "out": "out_hidden_size", "merge": "spatial_merge_size", "pos_n": "num_position_embeddings", "act": "hidden_act",
                  "temporal": "temporal_patch_size", "deepstack": "deepstack_visual_indexes"},
  "acts": {"gelu_pytorch_tanh": "gelu_tanh", "silu": "silu"},
  "patch_embed": {"weight": "patch_embed.proj.weight", "bias": "patch_embed.proj.bias"},
  "global": {
   "v.position_embd.weight": {"hf": "pos_embed.weight", "prep": "copy"},
   "v.post_ln.weight": {"hf": "merger.norm.weight", "prep": "copy"},
   "v.post_ln.bias": {"hf": "merger.norm.bias", "prep": "copy"},
   "mm.0.weight": {"hf": "merger.linear_fc1.weight"},
   "mm.0.bias": {"hf": "merger.linear_fc1.bias", "prep": "copy"},
   "mm.2.weight": {"hf": "merger.linear_fc2.weight"},
   "mm.2.bias": {"hf": "merger.linear_fc2.bias", "prep": "copy"}
  },
  "block": {
   "prefix": "blocks.{i}.",
   "tensors": {
    "ln1.weight": {"hf": "norm1.weight", "prep": "copy"}, "ln1.bias": {"hf": "norm1.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "ln2.weight": {"hf": "norm2.weight", "prep": "copy"}, "ln2.bias": {"hf": "norm2.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "attn_qkv.weight": {"hf": "attn.qkv.weight"}, "attn_qkv.bias": {"hf": "attn.qkv.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "attn_out.weight": {"hf": "attn.proj.weight"}, "attn_out.bias": {"hf": "attn.proj.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "ffn_up.weight": {"hf": "mlp.linear_fc1.weight"}, "ffn_up.bias": {"hf": "mlp.linear_fc1.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "ffn_down.weight": {"hf": "mlp.linear_fc2.weight"}, "ffn_down.bias": {"hf": "mlp.linear_fc2.bias", "prep": "copy"}
   }
  },
  "deepstack": {
   "prefix": "deepstack_merger_list.{k}.",
   "tensors": {
    "norm.weight": {"hf": "norm.weight", "prep": "copy"}, "norm.bias": {"hf": "norm.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "fc1.weight": {"hf": "linear_fc1.weight"}, "fc1.bias": {"hf": "linear_fc1.bias", "prep": "copy"},
    "fc2.weight": {"hf": "linear_fc2.weight"}, "fc2.bias": {"hf": "linear_fc2.bias", "prep": "copy"}
   }
  }
 },
 "semantics": {
  "rmsnorm": "(1 + w) * x / rms(x) (vLLM GemmaRMSNorm): every norm weight except linear_attn.norm.weight is stored zero-centred; the GGUF converter writes w + 1, here the prepare step adds 1 (op add1). linear_attn.norm is a plain gated RMSNorm weight (copy).",
  "A_log": "GGUF stores ssm_a = -exp(A_log) as f32 (op negexp).",
  "v_heads": "HF keeps the value heads grouped by key head (value head h reads key head h // (HV/HK), repeat_interleave); llama.cpp's converter reorders to tiled (h % HK) for ggml_repeat. The starter reads the HF order natively (cfg gdn.v_order grouped, gen_gdn.kh_line): no weight is permuted.",
  "conv1d": "HF [C, 1, K] bf16 == GGUF [C rows of K] f32 after a bf16 -> f32 copy.",
  "q_proj": "[heads * 2 * head_dim, hidden]: per head [query | gate] (attn_output_gate), the same packing as the GGUF's attn_q (cfg attn_gate fused_q).",
  "rope": "partial rotary (0.25 * head_dim = 64 of 256 dims), neox pairs, theta 1e7; mrope_section [11, 11, 10] interleaved only matters for image positions.",
  "mtp": "mtp.fc = eh_proj over concat(enorm(embed), hnorm(hidden)); mtp.norm = the head norm of the MTP block (nextn.shared_head_norm); one full-attention block with a dense FFN. All bf16 in the Quark export (kept as bf16 matrices)."
 }
